## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- The backend service must be running (see [Docker Setup Guide](./DOCKER_GUIDE.md))
- Default port: `8080`

### Health Check

Verify the backend is running:

```bash
curl http://localhost:8080/health
```

**Expected Response:**
```json
{
  "status": "ok",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-11T12:00:00Z"
}
```

---

## Authentication

> **Note:** Update this section based on your actual auth implementation (JWT, API Key, Session, etc.)

### JWT Authentication

Include the token in the `Authorization` header:

```
Authorization: Bearer <your-jwt-token>
```

### API Key Authentication

Include the key in the header:

```
X-API-Key: <your-api-key>
```

---

## API Endpoints

### Users

#### 1. Get All Users

| | |
|---|---|
| **Method** | `GET` |
| **URL** | `/api/users` |
| **Auth** | Required |

**Request:**
```bash
curl -X GET http://localhost:8080/api/users   -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"
```

**Query Parameters:**

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
| `page` | integer | No | Page number (default: 1) |
| `limit` | integer | No | Items per page (default: 10) |
| `search` | string | No | Search by name or email |

**Success Response (200 OK):**
```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "John Doe",
      "email": "john@example.com",
      "created_at": "2026-05-01T10:00:00Z"
    }
  ],
  "pagination": {
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 10,
    "total": 100,
    "total_pages": 10
  }
}
```

---

#### 2. Get User by ID

| | |
|---|---|
| **Method** | `GET` |
| **URL** | `/api/users/:id` |
| **Auth** | Required |

**Request:**
```bash
curl -X GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/1   -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"
```

**URL Parameters:**

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
| `id` | integer | Yes | User ID |

**Success Response (200 OK):**
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "avatar": "uploads/avatars/john.jpg",
  "created_at": "2026-05-01T10:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-05-10T14:30:00Z"
}
```

**Error Response (404 Not Found):**
```json
{
  "error": "User not found",
  "code": "USER_NOT_FOUND",
  "status": 404
}
```

---

#### 3. Create User

| | |
|---|---|
| **Method** | `POST` |
| **URL** | `/api/users` |
| **Auth** | Required |
| **Content-Type** | `application/json` |

**Request:**
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/users   -H "Content-Type: application/json"   -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"   -d '{
    "name": "Jane Smith",
    "email": "jane@example.com",
    "password": "securepassword123"
  }'
```

**Request Body:**

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| `name` | string | Yes | Full name (3-100 chars) |
| `email` | string | Yes | Valid email address |
| `password` | string | Yes | Min 8 characters |

**Success Response (201 Created):**
```json
{
  "id": 2,
  "name": "Jane Smith",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "created_at": "2026-05-11T12:00:00Z"
}
```

**Error Response (422 Unprocessable Entity):**
```json
{
  "error": "Validation failed",
  "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
  "status": 422,
  "details": {
    "email": ["Email is already taken"],
    "password": ["Password must be at least 8 characters"]
  }
}
```

---

#### 4. Update User

| | |
|---|---|
| **Method** | `PUT` |
| **URL** | `/api/users/:id` |
| **Auth** | Required |
| **Content-Type** | `application/json` |

**Request:**
```bash
curl -X PUT http://localhost:8080/api/users/1   -H "Content-Type: application/json"   -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"   -d '{
    "name": "John Updated",
    "email": "john.new@example.com"
  }'
```

**Success Response (200 OK):**
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "name": "John Updated",
  "email": "john.new@example.com",
  "updated_at": "2026-05-11T12:30:00Z"
}
```

---

#### 5. Delete User

| | |
|---|---|
| **Method** | `DELETE` |
| **URL** | `/api/users/:id` |
| **Auth** | Required |

**Request:**
```bash
curl -X DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/users/1   -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"
```

**Success Response (204 No Content)**

*(Empty body)*

---

### Posts

#### 6. Get All Posts

| | |
|---|---|
| **Method** | `GET` |
| **URL** | `/api/posts` |
| **Auth** | Optional / Public |

**Request:**
```bash
curl -X GET "http://localhost:8080/api/posts?page=1&limit=20&sort=created_at:desc"
```

**Query Parameters:**

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
| `page` | integer | No | Page number (default: 1) |
| `limit` | integer | No | Items per page (default: 20, max: 100) |
| `sort` | string | No | Sort field and order, e.g. `created_at:desc` |
| `author_id` | integer | No | Filter by author |
| `status` | string | No | Filter by status: `draft`, `published`, `archived` |

**Success Response (200 OK):**
```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Getting Started with Our API",
      "content": "This is the post content...",
      "author": {
        "id": 1,
        "name": "John Doe"
      },
      "status": "published",
      "created_at": "2026-05-10T10:00:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-05-10T10:00:00Z"
    }
  ],
  "pagination": {
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 20,
    "total": 50,
    "total_pages": 3
  }
}
```

---

#### 7. Get Post by ID

| | |
|---|---|
| **Method** | `GET` |
| **URL** | `/api/posts/:id` |
| **Auth** | Optional / Public |

**Request:**
```bash
curl -X GET http://localhost:8080/api/posts/1
```

**Success Response (200 OK):**
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Getting Started with Our API",
  "content": "This is the post content...",
  "author": {
    "id": 1,
    "name": "John Doe",
    "email": "john@example.com"
  },
  "status": "published",
  "tags": ["api", "tutorial"],
  "created_at": "2026-05-10T10:00:00Z"
}
```

---

#### 8. Create Post

| | |
|---|---|
| **Method** | `POST` |
| **URL** | `/api/posts` |
| **Auth** | Required |
| **Content-Type** | `application/json` |

**Request:**
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/posts   -H "Content-Type: application/json"   -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"   -d '{
    "title": "My New Post",
    "content": "This is the content of my post...",
    "status": "published",
    "tags": ["tutorial", "guide"]
  }'
```

**Request Body:**

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| `title` | string | Yes | Post title (5-200 chars) |
| `content` | string | Yes | Post content (min 10 chars) |
| `status` | string | No | `draft` or `published` (default: `draft`) |
| `tags` | array | No | Array of tag strings |

**Success Response (201 Created):**
```json
{
  "id": 2,
  "title": "My New Post",
  "content": "This is the content of my post...",
  "author_id": 1,
  "status": "published",
  "tags": ["tutorial", "guide"],
  "created_at": "2026-05-11T12:00:00Z"
}
```

---

#### 9. Update Post

| | |
|---|---|
| **Method** | `PUT` |
| **URL** | `/api/posts/:id` |
| **Auth** | Required (Owner or Admin) |
| **Content-Type** | `application/json` |

**Request:**
```bash
curl -X PUT http://localhost:8080/api/posts/2   -H "Content-Type: application/json"   -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"   -d '{
    "title": "Updated Post Title",
    "status": "published"
  }'
```

**Success Response (200 OK):**
```json
{
  "id": 2,
  "title": "Updated Post Title",
  "status": "published",
  "updated_at": "2026-05-11T12:30:00Z"
}
```

---

#### 10. Delete Post

| | |
|---|---|
| **Method** | `DELETE` |
| **URL** | `/api/posts/:id` |
| **Auth** | Required (Owner or Admin) |

**Request:**
```bash
curl -X DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/posts/2   -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"
```

**Success Response (204 No Content)**

---

### Uploads

#### 11. Upload File

| | |
|---|---|
| **Method** | `POST` |
| **URL** | `/api/uploads` |
| **Auth** | Required |
| **Content-Type** | `multipart/form-data` |

**Request:**
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/uploads   -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"   -F "file=@/path/to/your/image.jpg"   -F "folder=avatars"
```

**Form Data:**

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| `file` | file | Yes | File to upload (max 10MB) |
| `folder` | string | No | Target folder: `avatars`, `posts`, `general` |

**Success Response (201 Created):**
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "filename": "image.jpg",
  "original_name": "my-photo.jpg",
  "url": "http://localhost:8080/uploads/general/image.jpg",
  "size": 245760,
  "mime_type": "image/jpeg",
  "folder": "general",
  "uploaded_at": "2026-05-11T12:00:00Z"
}
```

**Error Response (413 Payload Too Large):**
```json
{
  "error": "File too large",
  "code": "FILE_TOO_LARGE",
  "status": 413,
  "max_size": "10MB"
}
```

---

#### 12. Get Upload by ID

| | |
|---|---|
| **Method** | `GET` |
| **URL** | `/api/uploads/:id` |
| **Auth** | Required |

**Request:**
```bash
curl -X GET http://localhost:8080/api/uploads/1   -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"
```

**Success Response (200 OK):**
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "filename": "image.jpg",
  "url": "http://localhost:8080/uploads/general/image.jpg",
  "size": 245760,
  "mime_type": "image/jpeg",
  "uploaded_at": "2026-05-11T12:00:00Z"
}
```

---

#### 13. Delete Upload

| | |
|---|---|
| **Method** | `DELETE` |
| **URL** | `/api/uploads/:id` |
| **Auth** | Required |

**Request:**
```bash
curl -X DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/uploads/1   -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>"
```

**Success Response (204 No Content)**

